usage: hdbread.py [-h] [--schema] [--ops] [--strings] [--mask] [--records] [--json] hdb

hdbread.py — read-only reader for Niagara N4 .hdb history files.

On-disk format, derived from the history-rt code (organized/history/history-rt/vineflower, N4; file:line):
  [0:4]   magic 0xA106F11E (-1593380578)          com/tridium/history/file/BFileHistoryTable.java:63,821
  [4:8]   file/history version (1 or 2)            BFileHistoryTable.java:128-130,821
  [8:12]  dataOffset: start of the data section,   BFileHistoryTable.java:821 (1600), :852-858 (doubled
          1600 unless the config needed more        while the config does not fit), :873 (read back)
  [12:dataOffset]  the HistoryConfig as BOG XML, space/zero padded (BFileHistoryTable.java:125-131,848-850)
  Fixed-length tables (a record type whose isFixedSize() is true: Numeric/Boolean/EnumTrendRecord,
  BNumericTrendRecord.java "isFixedSize ... return true") use com/tridium/history/file/fixed:
  [dataOffset : +28]  Header: 7 big-endian ints version(=1), pageSize, pageCount, recSize, capacity,
                      firstPage, lastPage   (fixed/Header.java:149-163); 64 bytes reserved (Header.SIZE)
  page i at dataOffset + 64 + i*pageSize   (fixed/PageManager.java:640-645); a page is first, last
                      (two ints, -1 = empty) then record j at 8 + j*recSize   (fixed/Page.java:38-40,60-66,89-91)
  page order: firstPage, next(i) = i+1 wrapping at pageCount, stop after lastPage
                      (fixed/Header.java next(), fixed/PageManager.java:583-587)
  record: timestamp, then status, trend flags and value (javax/baja/history/BHistoryRecord.java:96-99,
                      BTrendRecord.java:68-76,110-117):
    version 2: BAbsTime.decode48 = BAbsTime.decode: first byte b != 0 -> millis = ((b-16)&0xFF)<<40 | next
               5 bytes; b == 0 -> 8-byte form (baja/javax/baja/sys/BAbsTime.java:635-662); then status
               byte (BStatus bits) and trend-flags byte
    version 1: 8-byte millis (BAbsTime.encode = writeLong, BAbsTime.java:630-632), then one int:
               trendFlags << 24 | status bits (BTrendRecord.java:110-124)
    value: NumericTrendRecord float32 (BNumericTrendRecord.java:77-84), BooleanTrendRecord boolean byte
           (BBooleanTrendRecord.java:88-95), EnumTrendRecord int ordinal (BEnumTrendRecord.java:68-75)
  status names: BStatus support tags 1 disabled .. 128 unackedAlarm, "{ok}" when empty
                      (baja/javax/baja/sys/BStatus.java:287-290,354-357,484-491)
  trend flags: 1 start, 2 outOfOrder, 4 hidden, 8 modified, 16 interpolated, 32/64/128 reserved0-2,
               "{ }" when empty (javax/baja/history/BTrendFlags.java:155-158,244-251)
A header record size that differs from the size these rules give for the record type and version is
refused (HdbFormatError), never guessed. Audit/log records are variable-length (recstore/): --ops and
--strings walk them heuristically, --records does not decode them.

SECRETS DISCIPLINE: audit/log records carry operator activity. Use --mask to redact user identities
and long values before printing; cite structure/counts, not specific secret values.

Usage:
  python3 hdbread.py <file.hdb> [--schema] [--ops] [--strings] [--mask]
  python3 hdbread.py <file.hdb> --records [--json]   trend records as CSV (or JSON) on stdout,
        timestamp (UTC ISO 8601), millis, status, trendFlags, value; summary on stderr
  (no option = --schema). Exit 0 ok, 2 usage or an unreadable file, 1 a non-.hdb file, nothing decoded
  or a record format this reader does not decode.

positional arguments:
  hdb         a Niagara .hdb history file

options:
  -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  --schema    history id, record type and field list (default)
  --ops       count audit-log operation strings
  --strings   printable strings of the record region
  --mask      redact user identities and long values (--strings)
  --records   decode Numeric/Boolean/EnumTrendRecord rows: CSV on stdout, summary on stderr
  --json      with --records: a JSON list instead of CSV
